<title>USA: U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to watch - May 16.</title>
<headline>U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to watch - May 16.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>-- Hewlett-Packard Co reported an eight percent rise in net earnings for its second fiscal quarter but fell short of Wall Street expectations. H-P shares declined in London on the news.</p>
<p>-- Staples Inc reported operating earnings of $0.12 per share for the first quarter, versus $0.08 a year ago.</p>
<p>-- Pep Boys--Manny, Moe &amp; Jack reported higher first quarter earnings.  </p>
<p>-- Marvel Entertainment Group Inc reported a first quarter loss greater than a year ago. The company said trading card and toy revenues declined due to concerns over Chapter 11 proceedings.</p>
<p>-- St. Jude Medical said its chief financial officer plans to leave the company by month's end.</p>
<p>((--Wall Street Desk 212-859-1730))</p>
